meta {
  name: Buy
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/trade/buy/AAPL?quantity=1
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  quantity: 1
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Manual Buy

  Places a manual market BUY for testing the trading pipeline by hand. Goes
  through the same OrderService the strategies use, so all guardrails apply
  (trading-halt + buying-power checks). Recorded in the trade log as strategy
  "MANUAL". On success the position is registered/increased in the tracker so a
  later SELL is permitted by the no-short guardrail.

  ## Path / Query
  - `{ticker}` — equity symbol, case-insensitive (e.g. AAPL)
  - `quantity` — shares to buy (default 1)

  ## Responses
  - `200` — { side, ticker, quantity, success, orderId, message, orderRequest,
    webullHttpStatus, webullResponse, submittedToWebull, mode, heldAfter, timestamp }
  - `422` — guardrail rejection (e.g. TRADING_HALTED, INSUFFICIENT_BUYING_POWER)
  - `400` — invalid input (non-positive quantity)

  ## Debugging fields
  - `orderRequest` — the exact order payload we sent to Webull (order_type,
    quantity, prices, session, etc.). BUY uses order_type=MARKET.
  - `webullHttpStatus` — HTTP status from Webull (-1 = not sent / simulated / guardrail)
  - `webullResponse` — raw Webull success/failure body
  - `submittedToWebull` — true only when the order actually reached Webull

  ## Note
  Orders only reach Webull when webull.trading.submit-orders=true. POST places a
  REAL order in LIVE mode; sent to the sandbox in PAPER mode (with submit-orders).
}
